From 6631b221c117f3d4c901a5e2087a48fb9899be09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:58:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/52] Reattach to the remote shell when the PTY connection
 drops

Browsers close WebSockets on sleep and network changes, which left the panel
looking alive but dead. The host now keeps the shell running and sends a
session id; on a closed connection the event loop reconnects with it (backing
off up to 5 s), holds outgoing input while disconnected, and stops once the
host reports the shell exited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
